WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:00.960
- [Kelly] Welcome back, y'all.
(audience applauds)

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:03.480
I'm here with Niall Horan and
Kimberly Williams-Paisley.

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:04.313
Give it up, y'all.

00:00:04.313 --> 00:00:06.872
(audience cheers)
(Kelly claps)

00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:09.180
So my next guest comes to
you five mornings a week

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.030
on MSNBC as co-host of "Morning Joe".

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.640
She also is the founder
of Know Your Value,

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:17.670
a nationwide movement to
empower and support women.

00:00:17.670 --> 00:00:19.620
In 2020, they partnered with Forbes

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.530
to create the first ever 50 over 50 list

00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:24.120
to spotlight badass women

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.340
who have achieved success later in life.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:27.930
Please welcome, dialed in,

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:29.666
Mika Brzezinski, everybody!

00:00:29.666 --> 00:00:33.660
(audience cheers)
(upbeat music)

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:34.560
What's up Mika?

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.330
Say hi to Niall and Kimberly.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:37.620
- Hello.
- Hi, Mika.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:38.850
- Hi guys, hi Kimberly.

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:39.683
How are you?

00:00:39.683 --> 00:00:41.160
Hi Niall.
- [Niall] Hello.

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:42.659
- [Niall and Kelly] Hello.

00:00:42.659 --> 00:00:43.492
(all laugh)

00:00:43.492 --> 00:00:44.640
- So wait, I hear that you

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.410
and Jimmy Carter's daughter nearly caused

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:47.790
an international incident,

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:50.790
and I really need to know what that is.

00:00:50.790 --> 00:00:52.860
- Several, okay, so with Amy Carter,

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:55.500
it was at Camp David
during the peace accord,

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:57.540
and we were trying to ride a golf cart,

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:59.970
and we were way underage
to be driving anything,

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:03.630
and I hit the Israeli Prime
Minister Menachem Begin

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:04.683
with the golf cart.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.200
Luckily I didn't kill
him, just nicked him.

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.390
- Nicked him?
- So that was one.

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:10.440
There were many disasters.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.540
We had Deng Xiaoping, the leader of China,

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.331
over to our house for a state dinner

00:01:14.331 --> 00:01:15.630
in The Plains, Virginia,

00:01:15.630 --> 00:01:16.950
at our farmhouse.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:18.630
And I was serving caviar,

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:21.021
and I tripped and spilled it on his lap,

00:01:21.021 --> 00:01:22.650
and then,

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:23.850
I tried to wipe it off

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:24.690
- [Audience] Whoa.
- and, like,

00:01:24.690 --> 00:01:26.677
the Secretary of State
was next to him going,

00:01:26.677 --> 00:01:28.770
"Oh, just stop, just stop."

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:33.360
Like, disaster after disaster
growing up Brzezinski.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:34.590
International disaster.

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:38.625
- Oh my gosh, I love
you so much right now.

00:01:38.625 --> 00:01:39.458
(audience laughing)
Oh my God,

00:01:39.458 --> 00:01:40.291
I loved you before,

00:01:40.291 --> 00:01:42.270
but you have grown in my heart.

00:01:42.270 --> 00:01:44.460
So, Niall, have you ever
had any interesting moments

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:45.450
with world leaders?

00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:46.710
- I don't think I'm gonna tell my story

00:01:46.710 --> 00:01:47.543
after all of that.
- Wait, wait.

00:01:47.543 --> 00:01:49.140
You met the Queen though, didn't you?

00:01:49.140 --> 00:01:50.940
- Yeah, no, I've been lucky enough

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:54.330
to have met the Queen on a
couple of occasions actually.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:55.163
- Really?
- Yeah.

00:01:55.163 --> 00:01:57.510
It was as cool as you would think it is.

00:01:57.510 --> 00:01:59.100
- [Kelly] Okay.
- Such a nice woman

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:00.180
and her,

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:02.610
she has a massive
knowledge of horse racing.

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:03.930
She owns a lot of horses

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:06.015
and all of her jockeys were all Irish guys

00:02:06.015 --> 00:02:08.580
and they were there at
this thing we were at.

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:09.413
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:09.413 --> 00:02:10.246
- And she came over to
have a chat with them

00:02:10.246 --> 00:02:12.360
about the weekend's horse racing

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:13.560
and I was just like,
- [Kelly] Sure.

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:14.393
- Sick,

00:02:14.393 --> 00:02:16.620
the Queen is just chatting
horse racing right next to me,

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:17.910
which I thought was just really sweet.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:20.160
- Wait so when you meet her,
do you have to, like, curtsy?

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:21.450
- Yeah.
- Do you have to do something?

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:22.470
- You have to,

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:24.390
you're not allowed to speak
until you're spoken to.

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:25.223
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:02:25.223 --> 00:02:26.190
- You

00:02:26.190 --> 00:02:27.660
say "ma'am".

00:02:27.660 --> 00:02:28.493
Call her "ma'am,"

00:02:28.493 --> 00:02:29.326
"Her Majesty,"

00:02:29.326 --> 00:02:30.159
and then from there on,

00:02:30.159 --> 00:02:31.140
"ma'am."

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:31.973
I could have got this wrong.

00:02:31.973 --> 00:02:32.806
This was a while ago
- I know.

00:02:32.806 --> 00:02:34.170
- but something like this.
- Were you freaking out?

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:35.400
I would've been sweating.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:36.233
- They're coming up.

00:02:36.233 --> 00:02:37.920
They're telling you all
this before you meet her

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:39.521
and it's already a
scary experience meeting

00:02:39.521 --> 00:02:40.740
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:41.610
- Queen of England,

00:02:41.610 --> 00:02:43.650
probably the most famous
person on this planet.

00:02:43.650 --> 00:02:45.360
- Yeah, I feel like I
would've messed it up

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:46.193
and walked in and been like,

00:02:46.193 --> 00:02:47.026
"What's up?"

00:02:47.026 --> 00:02:47.859
And they would be like,
(Kelly yells)

00:02:47.859 --> 00:02:48.965
- Hey, y'all!

00:02:48.965 --> 00:02:50.658
(everyone laughs)

00:02:50.658 --> 00:02:52.349
- (indistinct) get Elly May outta here.

00:02:52.349 --> 00:02:53.580
(audience laughing)

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:54.630
Okay, so, Mika,

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:56.130
you created Know Your Value

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:58.140
to empower women of all backgrounds,

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:00.360
so what's a key lesson that you emphasize?

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.030
- Well, I created Know Your
Value, like, 12 years ago

00:03:03.030 --> 00:03:05.520
and I've been doing
events across the country

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:07.740
teaching women to know their value.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:11.220
Literally, how do you put
your value into words?

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:12.660
Women struggle with that.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:16.410
They tend to apologize and
self-deprecate themselves

00:03:16.410 --> 00:03:21.030
through job interviews or
promotional conversations

00:03:21.030 --> 00:03:24.300
and instead of advocating for themselves.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:25.133
And so,

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:27.720
we teach them how to collect
the data on themselves

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.390
but then also teach them techniques-

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:31.410
eye contact,

00:03:31.410 --> 00:03:32.243
posture,

00:03:32.243 --> 00:03:33.420
presentation,

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:34.253
dress-

00:03:34.253 --> 00:03:37.260
all the things that keep
your message cohesive

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:39.990
and communicate your value effectively.

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:42.600
And I found that women
really struggle with this

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:44.190
and there's a huge need

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:45.780
for Know Your Value.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:46.650
- Yeah, it's so funny.

00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:47.940
I mean, I'm the first person to,

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:49.860
I'm so self-deprecating and I make a joke

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.450
and we're trained, like,

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:52.283
from childhood,

00:03:52.283 --> 00:03:53.550
especially in the South, like,

00:03:53.550 --> 00:03:56.220
to just not kind of be
in the way and, like,

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:57.053
it's just,

00:03:57.053 --> 00:03:57.886
it's innate in you

00:03:57.886 --> 00:03:59.310
and you don't even
realize you're doing it.

00:03:59.310 --> 00:04:00.480
Do you feel like,

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:01.313
I don't know,

00:04:01.313 --> 00:04:02.146
is there something you would've told

00:04:02.146 --> 00:04:03.090
the younger version of you?

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.520
Like maybe don't do this or do this?

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:08.680
- Yeah, I literally can't put
my value into words right now.

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:12.780
(everyone laughs)
(Kelly claps)

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:16.590
- That's not funny, but it is.
(everyone laughs)

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:17.671
- She made the joke,

00:04:17.671 --> 00:04:18.547
so it's fine for us to laugh.

00:04:18.547 --> 00:04:20.730
- It's okay for us to laugh.
(everyone laughs)

00:04:20.730 --> 00:04:22.990
No, but I feel like I would've
told myself many things.

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:23.823
- Yeah, I mean like,

00:04:23.823 --> 00:04:25.590
I wish that I knew how to
deal with stress better

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:26.490
as a younger kid.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:27.480
Like, you know,

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:28.920
how to manage that

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.360
and let it go through you

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:31.380
and let it go and then,

00:04:31.380 --> 00:04:33.540
yeah and learn your value.

00:04:33.540 --> 00:04:35.160
- Yeah, I think that's
a really fair point.

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:35.993
Well, Mika,

00:04:35.993 --> 00:04:36.840
you helped create-

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:37.673
this is so cool-

00:04:37.673 --> 00:04:39.360
the 50 over 50 lists with Forbes.

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.370
So why was this important for you?

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:42.210
- Well, actually,

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:44.760
it's for everything Kimberly
was just talking about.

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:45.750
50 over 50,

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:47.730
the list I created with Forbes,

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:50.790
is actually a great
message for younger women.

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.880
What I would've loved to
have told my younger self is

00:04:53.880 --> 00:04:56.160
that we have a long runway.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.650
What we discovered creating
the 50 over 50 list,

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:01.500
which immediately went global,

00:05:01.500 --> 00:05:04.410
because there were so
many women nominating,

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:05.730
putting in nominations.

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:07.687
Some women trying to
lie up and we're like,

00:05:07.687 --> 00:05:09.420
"Sorry, you're 49.
(clicks tongue)

00:05:09.420 --> 00:05:10.290
Can't make it."

00:05:10.290 --> 00:05:12.870
But this list showed me
that there are women,

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:13.703
many women,

00:05:13.703 --> 00:05:15.300
having amazing impact

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:16.710
and making a lot of money

00:05:16.710 --> 00:05:20.820
well after 50, 60, 70, 80, and 90.

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:23.257
And the message for younger women is,

00:05:23.257 --> 00:05:25.230
"You've got a long runway.

00:05:25.230 --> 00:05:28.110
We've paved it for you so you can relax

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:29.250
and enjoy the moment

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:30.960
and slow down

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:32.310
and try and do things right

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:33.651
and make those mistakes

00:05:33.651 --> 00:05:36.780
and experience those experiences.

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:38.070
Be there for them

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:40.980
so that each one can
build upon the other."

00:05:40.980 --> 00:05:43.920
I spent a lot of my younger years rushing

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:46.290
and a lot of bringing
up my kids and working,

00:05:46.290 --> 00:05:47.160
rushing,

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:49.630
not knowing that this runway existed.

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:53.250
The list is an incredible
message to younger women.

00:05:53.250 --> 00:05:54.083
- Absolutely.

00:05:54.083 --> 00:05:54.916
I think you've just found, like,

00:05:54.916 --> 00:05:57.619
the one place a woman will
lie and say she's older.

00:05:57.619 --> 00:05:58.620
(everyone laughing)

00:05:58.620 --> 00:05:59.887
I don't know any woman that's like,

00:05:59.887 --> 00:06:01.257
"I'm older than I am."

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:03.633
Congratulations.

